```c
static void MixColumns_hls(state_t state) {
  uint8_t i;
  #pragma hls_unroll yes
  for (i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    uint8_t s0 = state[i][0];
    uint8_t s1 = state[i][1];
    uint8_t s2 = state[i][2];
    uint8_t s3 = state[i][3];
    
    uint8_t Tmp = s0 ^ s1 ^ s2 ^ s3;
    
    uint8_t Tm0 = xtime(s0 ^ s1);
    uint8_t Tm1 = xtime(s1 ^ s2);
    uint8_t Tm2 = xtime(s2 ^ s3);
    uint8_t Tm3 = xtime(s3 ^ s0);

    #pragma hls_pipeline_init_interval 1
    state[i][0] ^= Tm0 ^ Tmp;
    state[i][1] ^= Tm1 ^ Tmp;
    state[i][2] ^= Tm2 ^ Tmp;
    state[i][3] ^= Tm3 ^ Tmp;
  }
}

static void MixColumns(state_t *state) {
  MixColumns_hls(*state);
}
```

Key optimizations:
1. Maintained full loop unrolling for maximum parallelism
2. Introduced local variables (s0-s3) to reduce state array accesses
3. Parallelized all xtime computations before state updates
4. Added pipeline pragma with II=1 for the final XOR operations to enable temporal parallelism
5. Removed intermediate variables to simplify dataflow

This version exposes more operation-level parallelism while maintaining strict latency focus through full unrolling. The pipeline pragma helps overlap operations that couldn't be parallelized through unrolling alone.
